Training a Boerboel requires early consitency, firm leardership, and positive reinforcement because these dogs grow into immensely strong and protective adults.

Start Early: Begin socialization and basic obedience between 8 to 16 weeks of age to shape stable adults behavior.

Use positive Reinforcement: Reward for good behavior with small, high-value treats and praise Boerboels are smart and eager to please their owners.

Set firm boundries: Maintain calm , confident leardership. Use a gentle yet firm approach rather than harsh punishment that break trust.

Incoporate Structure: Apply protocols like Nothing in Life Is Free from day one to manage dominace and establish clear rules. 
